  pages={1-5},
  abstract={Crude oil prices are influenced by geopolitical, economic, and psychological factors, making accurate prediction and robust trading challenging. This paper proposes an AI-based trading system that integrates machine learning with sentiment analysis from news and social media, supported by systematic risk management. Using historical WTI crude oil prices and sentiment data (2015-2025), predictive features are engineered and a novel Sentiment-Conditioned Random Forest with dynamic trade sizing and volatility filters is applied. The model achieves an annualized return of $\mathbf{1 8. 5 \%}$ and a Sharpe ratio of $\mathbf{1. 4 2}$, outperforming conventional technical strategies. The framework fuses multi-source financial data (market/news/events), enables trade sizing through confidence-sentiment alignment, and embeds realtime risk controls-advancing beyond static RF approaches. It combines feature engineering, model selection, execution, and compliance-aware overlays into a single pipeline. Emphasizing explainability, adaptability, and modularity, this work presents a practical architecture for AI-based commodity trading under volatile market conditions.},
  keywords={Training;Adaptation models;Sentiment analysis;Uncertainty;Oils;Trees (botanical);Pipelines;Data models;Risk management;Random forests;AI trading;crude oil;sentiment analysis;machine learning;risk management;market volatility;regulatory measures},
