  year={2025},
  volume={},
  number={},
  pages={283-288},
  abstract={Geopolitical crises and economic volatility create uncertainty, underscoring the need for reliable gold price forecasting as a safe-haven asset. This study compares the performance of traditional regression (SARIMAX, VAR, and GARCH) and deep learning (LSTM, BiLSTM, and GRU) models, along with a hybrid approach, for predicting one-month-ahead gold prices. We utilize 25 years of monthly data and implemented feature selection to identify the top 10 most influential factors, including macroeconomic indicators (e.g., S&P 500, Crude Oil) and the Geopolitical Risk Index. A hybrid model was developed by optimising the VAR forecasting results, which were optimised by utilising their residuals as input for the LSTM model, and then re-integrating them to obtain more accurate gold price forecasting results, with a MAE of 78.21, MSE of 10,180.10, RMSE of 100.89, MAPE of 4.79%, and $\mathbf{R}^{\mathbf{2}}$ of 95.37%. The results were also confirmed by the Diebold Mariano Test, where the hybrid model had a stats value of -12.66 compared to the basic VAR model, which was the best regression model in this study. The findings validate the use of combined macroeconomic and geopolitical data for gold price prediction and provide comparative performance metrics to guide model selection.},
