  pages={1648-1653},
  abstract={The international financial system relies heavily upon gold, both as a main source of investment and also as a hedge against unpredictable changes. The large demand for this specific asset along with its fluctuating price (based upon an ever-increasing number of variables) makes accurate forecasting a challenging issue; these variables are defined by future inflation rates, currency fluctuation rates, and changes in political landscapes. Traditionally, financial analysts utilize Linear Regression, Decision Tree, and Random Forest, derive inferences by interpreting complex transactional relationships. However, the aforementioned models typically under-represent the time-dependent nature of financial time-series data. Our ML model/algorithm is a multi-modal hybrid deep learning model combining Convolutional Neural Networks (CNN) to extract static numerical sequences used for making decisions with Long Term (LSTM) Memory Networks. This was done to overcome the limitations related to using only static numeric data. This model utilizes both structured macroeconomic indicator data in addition to real-time sentiment analysis of global financial markets, from relevant news articles, to generate decisions as input data. We conducted experimental evaluation in order to benchmark our multi-modal hybrid design against several traditional ensemble-classifiers; and observed that there was an average decrease of 4.5% in RMSE and an increase of 6.8% in R-Squared for our architecture compared to the other classifiers. Additionally, we demonstrated the ability for real-time forecasting and dynamic risk visualization via a cloud-based interactive interface; thereby supporting our claim that we have produced a valid and reliable decision support tool in the context of rapidly evolving and highly volatile financial markets.},
