  title={A Hybrid CNN-BiLSTM-Attention Model for Enhanced Electrical Load Forecasting in Bangladesh}, 
  year={2025},
  volume={},
  number={},
  pages={3929-3933},
  abstract={Reliable load forecasting is essential for efficient power grid operation, ensuring supply–demand balance, and supporting energy market decisions. However, electricity demand time series often exhibit volatility, seasonal fluctuations, and nonlinear relationships, which limit the effectiveness of traditional forecasting approaches. To address this, this paper introduces a hybrid deep learning framework, termed CNN–BiLSTM–Attention, designed for enhanced load prediction. The model integrates three components: a Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) to capture local patterns, a Bidirectional Long Short-Term Memory (BiLSTM) to learn temporal dependencies, and an Attention mechanism to emphasize the most relevant time steps. The proposed approach was tested on a real-world energy demand dataset and compared with standard BiLSTM and CNN–BiLSTM models. Experimental findings reveal that the proposed model outperforms BiLSTM and CNN–BiLSTM baselines, achieving substantially lower error and stronger fit. These outcomes highlight the benefit of integrating convolutional feature extraction with attention-guided temporal modeling to achieve robust and precise electrical load forecasting.},
  keywords={Filtering;Filters;Circuits and systems;Protocols;HTTP;MISO;Radio access networks;Regional area networks;Attention mechanisms;Bidirectional long short term memory;Electrical Load Forecasting;Time Series Analysis;Convolutional Neural Network (CNN);Bidirectional LSTM (BiLSTM);Attention Mechanism},
